  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Bash Usage Audit for Validate Design",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Scope",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This audit synthesizes existing bash hardening evidence, tool-usage aggregates, validator scripts, and test surfaces to design a deterministic `validate` tool. It does not implement `validate`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Evidence Sources",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `docs/audits/tool-usage-analysis/tool-usage-summary.md` - `docs/audits/tool-usage-analysis/tool-usage-aggregates.json` - `docs/audits/tool-hardening/bash-deterministic-envelope.md` - `docs/audits/tool-hardening/search-replace-patch-contract.md` - `scripts/rig_relay_validate_schemas.py` - `scripts/rig_relay_validate_tool_receipts.py` - `tests/tools/test_bash.py` - `tests/tools/test_bash_hardening.py` - `tests/tools/test_validation_suite.py` - `tests/tools/test_tool_receipt_emission.py`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "What the Current Data Says",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The local tool-usage audit shows bash is the dominant high-authority command surface.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-8",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Metric",
        "Value"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Calls",
          "5,023"
        ],
        [
          "Failures",
          "337"
        ],
        [
          "Failure rate",
          "6.71%"
        ],
        [
          "p95 latency",
          "10,469 ms"
        ],
        [
          "p95 output",
          "8,012 bytes"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The strongest empirical signal is not raw command text. It is command family pressure:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- validation commands are frequent and already script-shaped - inspection commands are frequent and mostly read-only - Git introspection is common and high-authority - schema and receipt validation already exist as standalone scripts - mutation commands are already separated by tool boundaries, so bash should not become a general mutation gateway",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Command Categories",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Validation / Test Execution",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Observed command family:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `uv run pytest` - `uv run pytest tests/...` - `uv run pytest -n0 ...` - `uv run pyright ...` - `uv run ruff check ...` - `uv run ruff format ...` - `uv run ruff format --check ...` - `uv run python scripts/rig_relay_validate_schemas.py` - `uv run python scripts/rig_relay_validate_tool_receipts.py ...`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Empirical role:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- high frequency in this repo - deterministic enough to model as first-class validate profiles - mostly read-only, with clear pass/fail semantics",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recommendation:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- absorb into `validate` - keep bash fallback for ad hoc or one-off command composition",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Git Introspection",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Observed command family:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `git status` - `git diff` - `git log` - `git show` - `git ls-files` - `git branch`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Empirical role:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- read-only but high leverage - used for promotion/readiness and dirty-state checks - should be deterministic and content-light",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recommendation:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- absorb into `validate` for readiness checks - later migrate to a dedicated deterministic Git-read surface if needed",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "File / Content Inspection",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Observed command family:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `rg ...` - `find ...` - `ls ...` - `sed ...` - `jq ...` - `du ...` - `stat ...`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Empirical role:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- common inspection layer - low mutation risk - useful for audits and repository discovery",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recommendation:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- keep bash for ad hoc inspection - absorb only repeatable read-only checks into `validate`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Report / Dataset Generation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Observed command family:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `uv run python scripts/rig_relay_*.py` - validation and export scripts",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Empirical role:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- deterministic pipeline steps - often depends on a known repo root or evidence root",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recommendation:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- absorb fixed report-generation checks into `validate` - keep free-form report generation in bash when it is exploratory",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-40",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Mutation / Destructive / Refused Commands",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Observed command family:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- repo mutation commands - file edits - Git write operations - cleanup / pruning / archive operations",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Empirical role:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- should not be the default validate target - usually need a separate governed tool or explicit mutation surface",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recommendation:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- exclude from `validate` by default - gate via explicit mutation profiles if they ever become eligible",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-47",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Validate Absorption Rules",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`validate` should absorb commands when all are true:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- command is deterministic or close to deterministic - exit code is enough to decide pass/fail - output can be summarized content-light - command is read-only or check-only - the command is a repeated workflow primitive, not a one-off exploration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`validate` should stay out of bash when any are true:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- command is exploratory or ad hoc - command is interactive - command depends on arbitrary shell expansion - command mutates state - command needs raw stdout as the main product",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-52",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Gaps in Current Data",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- raw bash command text is not preserved in the content-light observability stream - exact command-family counts are therefore partially inferred from validator scripts and hardening docs - failure classification for bash commands is still mostly external to the command text - no canonical `command_kind` field exists yet",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-54",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Conclusion",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The strongest `validate` candidates are:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. `pytest` 2. `pyright` 3. `ruff check` 4. schema validation scripts 5. receipt-policy validation scripts 6. git cleanliness / readiness checks",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These are the commands most likely to benefit from deterministic profiles, structured receipts, and blocker taxonomy.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
